{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9ozrwibvj","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Product positioning — validated differentiators from real usage","summary":"Three strong differentiators confirmed through first-hand product use:\n\n1. **Main thread stays unblocked** — classifier + gate enforcing subagent dispatch means the main agent conversation never blocks and the main context window stays open. This is a concrete, felt UX benefit.\n\n2. **Task visibility + token consumption** — real-time observability into in-flight tasks and token cost is genuinely useful. Surfaces what's happening without requiring the user to dig.\n\n3. **Self-learning loop** — unexpectedly powerful; solved real problems the user didn't anticipate, including metric convergence — a problem the user didn't think the loop would address. This is a flagship differentiator worth leading on in positioning.\n\nThese are not theoretical; they emerged from real usage friction and surprise. Lean into #1 and #3 in positioning materials — they are the least obvious and most defensible.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T16:08:46.338Z","vec":[-0.0754280611872673,-0.043091364204883575,-0.040283966809511185,-0.08956233412027359,0.0285006295889616,-0.03932378441095352,0.08278872072696686,0.04785477742552757,0.03868875652551651,-0.01035595964640379,0.031182698905467987,0.061066802591085434,-0.026227664202451706,-0.027624281123280525,-0.004148480482399464,-0.002997962525114417,0.07251891493797302,0.05734340846538544,-0.019605249166488647,0.008119259960949421,0.044296033680438995,-0.03416619822382927,0.021484054625034332,0.06642753630876541,-0.08858302235603333,0.11449495702981949,-0.049090705811977386,-0.014978419989347458,0.10351647436618805,-0.10875198990106583,0.023985732346773148,0.031001310795545578,-0.0009862602455541492,-0.051746293902397156,-0.01885933242738247,0.030772441998124123,-0.01600823365151882,0.028529077768325806,-0.03992944210767746,-0.00034617556957527995,-0.01128530